## Parser Issue: Month-first parser, day-first tenants

**393 reports** from ticket #4471

The shared date parser reads all dates with month first. Tenants in day-first locales (en-GB, it-IT, de-DE, etc.) type dates as DD/MM, but the parser interprets them as MM/DD, causing a consistent inversion.

<Callout>
Root cause identified. Fix queued. GitHub issue: #11
</Callout>

### How it fails

- User in Italy books appointment for "12/3" (March 12 in DD/MM format)
- Parser reads "12/3" as "month 12, day 3" (December 3)
- Date flips every time it passes through the parser
- Bookings, invites, and reminders all show the wrong date

### Impact by channel

- App reports: ~186
- Email reports: ~159
- Form reports: ~48

### Affected locales

en-GB, en-IE, it-IT, fr-FR, de-DE, nl-NL, da-DK, pt-PT, es-ES, pl-PL, cs-CZ

### Root cause

The parser was written for MM/DD-first locales and never updated to respect locale-specific date conventions via `Intl.DateTimeFormat` or similar.

### Fix approach

1. Detect tenant locale in booking/invite pipeline
2. Use locale-aware date parsing (Intl API)
3. Ensure all date conversions respect the locale's natural date order

### GitHub issue

[#11: Parser issue (393 reports) — month-first parser, day-first tenants](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/11)

